From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3576: let the NPU power domain own vdd_npu_s0

Round 379 measured an idle charsiu session and found both NPU cores
runtime-suspended with zero active time, which is right, and the NPU rail
sitting at 750 mV anyway, which is not.

rocket's runtime_suspend does clk_bulk_disable_unprepare and nothing else;
there is no regulator call anywhere in drivers/accel/rocket. A rail follows
the domain only through domain-supply on the power-domain node, taken by
rockchip_pd_power(), and only when the domain carries need_regulator.

The driver half was already in this tree: DOMAIN_RK3576_R exists and
RK3576_PD_NPU already uses it. The DTS was the half that never caught up,
so the rail could not drop no matter what the domain did.

Three lines, and the same ones v9 posts upstream:

  - label the domain so a board file can reach it
  - drop regulator-always-on from vdd_npu_s0 only, leaving the other
    thirty-three always-on regulators alone
  - hand the rail to the domain

Both NPU cores stay enabled, which is where this board differs from the
posted DTS on purpose: charsiu's int4 decode needs both.

The domains and the clocks were already dropping, so what this recovers is
the buck's quiescent draw plus leakage into gated logic. That is real but
small, and this board cannot measure it -- it has no INA, no shunt and no
fuel gauge. No wattage is claimed. "Small but forever" is the category that
matters on a battery, and the fix was already written.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
index 11416ed12..73bc3cb68 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
@@ -442,7 +442,6 @@ regulator-state-mem {
 			};
 
 			vdd_npu_s0: dcdc-reg2 {
-				regulator-always-on;
 				regulator-boot-on;
 				regulator-enable-ramp-delay = <400>;
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <550000>;
@@ -723,6 +722,10 @@ &pcie0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pd_npu {
+	domain-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+};
+
 &pinctrl {
 	hdmi {
 		hdmi_tx_on_h: hdmi-tx-on-h {
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
index 66544b4d3..4997b880e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
@@ -1042,7 +1042,7 @@ power: power-controller {
 				#address-cells = <1>;
 				#size-cells = <0>;
 
-				power-domain@RK3576_PD_NPU {
+				pd_npu: power-domain@RK3576_PD_NPU {
 					reg = <RK3576_PD_NPU>;
 					#power-domain-cells = <1>;
 					#address-cells = <1>;
